what's going on guys this is rob and we  are back with another installment of our  beyond omega level series where we  discuss the most powerful characters in  comics and today we're diving into the  dc universe specifically the green  lantern lore and discussing the  guardians of the universe so the  guardians of the universe were created  by john broom and gil kane and first  appeared in green lantern number one in  1960. now the guardians are one of the  oldest races in the entire universe and  originally lived on a planet called  maltis and looked essentially like blue  humans now they valued science learning  and discovery above everything else and  one fateful day one resident of maltest  named krona was experimenting with time  manipulation to try and observe the  universe's origin which resulted in the  universe being split up into several  different universes that would make up  the dc multiverse and so resulted in the  creation of court a universe made of  antimatter which is where the  anti-monitor was said to be from before  dc retconned that now to try and atone  for creating a chaotic disorganized  universe the residents of malta leave  their home planet and take up residence  on owa a planet at the center of the  universe itself and it's on owa that  some of the maltrusions become the  guardians of the universe devoted to  preserving law and order in the universe  itself and they also get a lot shorter  and their heads get a lot bigger for  some reason but regardless the  guardian's first attempt at keeping  peace in the galaxy came in the form of  the man hunters which were basically an  android police force that the guardians  created and that worked pretty well for  a few million years until something went  wrong with the programming of the  manhunters and they rebelled against the  guardians and began killing people  instead of protecting them now after the  guardians defeat the rogue man hunters  they decommission the rest of them and  get to work on creating a replacement  police force now the reality here is the  reason why the manhunter's programming  went awry is because cronus screwed with  him but not wanting a repeat of the man  hunters the guardians decided that they  actually needed to use living beings  this time so to that end they create the  green lantern corps now members of the  green lantern corps are chosen based on  their willpower by power rings that get  their power from perhaps the greatest  scientific achievement of the maltusions  the central power battery located on owa  which basically powers the rings through  smaller batteries or lanterns that each  member of the green lantern corps  carries with them and the fact that the  guardians created the green lantern  corps is really all the evidence we need  that they are beyond omega level because  the green lanterns themselves are  powerful enough to be considered omega  level and at this point in a video about  pretty much any dc character i usually  have to explain how all of this was  changed by the various reboots that dc's  done over the years but thankfully the  green lantern mythos has largely  remained unchanged by both christ's  undefined earth and the new 52 the only  real big difference here is that instead  of the guardians of the universe just  being able to tap into the emotional  spectrum arbitrarily one day instead it  was the first lantern vault thumb a guy  from an alternate reality that taught  them how to do that now they attempted  to create a lantern by using volthume  and then everything went belly up but  that's how they learned to tie or at  least to access the emotional spectrum  was through vulthum the first lantern  and that actually came out of the green  lantern new 52 run but in terms of  powers the guardians have so many  abilities that listing them all is quite  difficult but i'll try to cover most of  them here so first of all they're  virtually immortal insofar as they would  likely live forever but they can die in  fact almost all of the guardians of the  universe did die during the events of  emerald twilight which took place in  green lantern issues 48-50 in 1994 where  hal jordan famously becomes the villain  known as parallax now this event sees  how jordan rebuild coast city after it  had been destroyed which is a violation  of the lantern corps rules and brings  him into conflict with the guardians now  this makes hal really pissed off and he  goes to owa to steal the central power  battery's energy to rebuild coast city  causing the guardians to release former  green lantern sinestro from his  imprisonment in the battery to try and  stop how now sinestro is eventually  killed by hal who also kills his former  teammate kilowatt and so in a last-ditch  effort to stop howe the guardians  transfer all their energy to one of  their members ganthet who becomes the  sole survivor of the guardians while the  rest of them die as well now shortly  thereafter while hal is still parallax  he battles green lantern kyle raynor and  the battle eventually destroys owa  itself but both owa and the guardians  are restored by kyle rayner recharging  the central power battery now in  addition to immortality the guardians of  the universe also possess near  omniscience and cosmic awareness as well  as vast telepathic and telekinetic  abilities the guardians are also able to  create and control hard light constructs  just like the green lanterns but to an  even more advanced degree with the  guardians having created constructs  strong enough to restrain sinestro as  well as the green lantern jon stewart  furthermore they are durable to the  point of being practically invulnerable  and can phase teleport and create  illusions and honestly the way they've  been depicted it seems like they're  basically omnipotent with the ability to  manipulate time matter and energy to the  point of being able to alter reality  itself now just to run over a few of the  feats the guardians of the universe have  done ganfit was able to destroy kilowog  a ridiculously powerful green lantern  with relative ease and was able to  incapacitate multiple green lanterns  simultaneously ganthet was also able to  damage some incredibly powerful enemies  including superboy prime although doing  so resulted in gandit's destruction he  was also able to harm the anti-monitor  and according to kyle raynor could  destroy a planet with merely a single  thought the guardians also displayed  vast abilities to manipulate genetics as  they actually gave the martian race  their weakness to fire to prevent a  segment of the martians the burning  martians themselves who were constantly  on fire from achieving space travel and  conquering other planets the guardians  were also able to imprison parallax the  embodiment of fear in the dc universe  within the central power battery and  were able to open a portal leading to  the afterlife they've shown the ability  to realign planets and stars and reverse  quantum singularities which are  basically points of entropy or chaos  which threaten the existence of the  universe itself the guardians were also  responsible for the creation of an  entire species when their experiments on  maltose and reptiles resulted in the  evolution of the scion race which would  themselves become a highly advanced  society so despite looking like little  blue oompa loompas the guardians of the  universe are quite powerful although  they sometimes suffer from being used in  storylines to be defeated by some really  powerful villain to show how powerful  that villain is still the fact that they  can destroy planets with a thought  definitely lets us know that they are  beyond omega level not to mention the  fact that they are able to control all  of the forces of the universe time  energy matter and reality itself so if  you guys enjoyed this video let me know  down in the comment section and as  always let me know who it is that you  want to see thank you all for watching  and i will catch you all later  peace
 

